robot-browser (3.6.10-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * The page can be drawn larger than it asks to be. The remote page belongs to
    somebody else and is laid out for a desk, while a terminal is a small panel
    an operator reads standing up at arm's length - so an operator sets the text
    size at the terminal, in Info, with the page resizing as the buttons are
    pressed. Remembered per terminal and re-applied after every load.
  * WB_PAGE_ZOOM in browser.config, or --zoom=, sets the size a deployment
    starts at; a size chosen at the terminal overrides it there.

 -- Jan Zwiegers <jan@radicalsystems.co.za>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0200

